  "notes": "{屈|かが}む describes bending the upper body forward or downward — stooping, crouching, or hunching.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n- Pair: {屈|かが}める (transitive: to bend something)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{屈|かが}んでいる means being in a stooped or crouched position.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {腰|こし}を{屈|かが}める: to bend at the waist (uses transitive form)\n- {身|み}を{屈|かが}める: to stoop, to duck\n- {前|まえ}{屈|かが}み: bending forward (noun)\n- {背中|せなか}が{屈|かが}んでいる: having a hunched back\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- しゃがむ: to squat, to crouch down (legs bend, body lowers)\n- {屈|かが}む: to stoop, to bend (upper body bends forward)",
